DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270123T075900Z
DTEND:20270123T085900Z
SUMMARY:[Healthcare & Clinical AI][Biomedical Imaging] AIiH 2027 - Special 
 session proposals
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on AI in Healthcare\
 nWebsite: https://aiih.cc/\nSource URL: https://aiih.cc/important-dates/\
 nLocation: Oxford\, United Kingdom\nTopics: Healthcare & Clinical AI\, Bi
 omedical Imaging\, Machine Learning\, Signal Processing\nSize: M\nSubmiss
 ion type: Full papers (double-blind\, proceedings) or abstracts (posters/
 spotlights\, Zenodo)\; late-breaking abstracts and STARS surveys\nConfide
 nce: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-29\nNotes: Official AIiH pages
  (checked 2026-10-29) list the fourth edition at the Mathematical Institu
 te\, University of Oxford\, Sep 1-3\, 2027\; the format is not stated. De
 adlines are published as 11.59PM Pacific Time (GMT-8) and stored at -08:0
 0\, although Pacific clocks are on GMT-7 from March\, so submit an hour e
 arly. Full papers are double-blind via CMT (2026 papers appeared in Sprin
 ger LNCS)\; abstracts and STARS surveys are archived on Zenodo. Size is a
 n editorial estimate.\nScope: Artificial intelligence for healthcare and 
 medicine\, including predictive analytics\, early diagnosis and preventio
 n\, machine and deep learning on health data\, AI-aided medical signal pr
 ocessing and imaging\, digital pathology and neurology\, drug discovery\,
  digital twins and precision medicine. Ethics\, patient data privacy and 
 patient-centred deployment are recurring themes. Original research papers
 \, abstracts and state-of-the-art surveys are accepted.\nAdditional topic
 s: Ethics & Governance\, Privacy-preserving ML\, Human-AI Interaction & D
 eployment\nScope sources (2027): https://aiih.cc/call-for-papers/\, https
 ://aiih.cc/call-for-stars/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-29
URL:https://aiih.cc/important-dates/
END:VEVENT
